{"term":"radish","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:132512f74ceef74df9","definition":"A plant of the Brassicaceae family, Raphanus sativus or Raphanus raphanistrum subsp. sativus, having an edible root.","example":"Many times they ſow divers ſeeds in a Bed together, as Radiſhes and Carrots, that by ſuch time as the Carrots come up, the Radiſhes may be gone. Upon beds newly ſet with Licorice they ſow Onions or Radiſh, or Lettice if their Licorice plants or ground be but weak, ſo as not quickly to cauſe a ſhadow with their leaves.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["beauty heart radish","beet radish","black radish","Chinese green radish","Chinese radish","Chinese white radish","common radish","daikon radish","European radish","fodder radish","forage radish","giant white radish","horseradish","horse-radish","icicle radish","Japanese radish","Korean radish","long white radish","oil radish","oilseed radish","oriental radish","Oriental radish","radish cake","radishless","radishlike","radish ripper","radishy","rat-tail radish","rattail radish","Ravensthorpe radish"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radish#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:eee3e42fae0c6f01cd","definition":"The root of this plant used as food. Some varieties are pungent and usually eaten raw in salads, etc., while others have a milder taste and are cooked.","example":"Fat people ſhould not eat freely of oily, nouriſhing diet. They ought frequently to eat radiſh, garlic, ſpices, or ſuch things as are heating, and promote perſpiration and urine.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["beauty heart radish","beet radish","black radish","Chinese green radish","Chinese radish","Chinese white radish","common radish","daikon radish","European ra